($q$How to Plan a Business Website That Brings in Enquiries$q$, $q$plan-a-business-website$q$, $q$Before you hire a developer, settle the goal, the pages and the content. A short planning checklist for a website that actually works.$q$, $q$<h2>Start with one clear goal</h2>
<p>A website that tries to do everything usually does nothing well. Decide the main action you want visitors to take: call you, fill a form, order a product or book a visit. Every page should support that goal.</p>
<p>Write the goal in one sentence and share it with anyone working on the site. It becomes the test for every design and content decision.</p>
<h2>List the pages you actually need</h2>
<p>Most small business sites need only a handful of pages, and each one should answer a question a customer really asks.</p>
<ul><li>Home: who you are, what you do and the next step</li><li>Services or products: one page per major service works best for search</li><li>About: the people and the story behind the business</li><li>Projects or clients: proof that you deliver</li><li>Contact: phone, email, address, map and a simple form</li></ul>
<h2>Prepare content before design begins</h2>
<p>Design goes faster and looks better when real text and images exist. Gather your service descriptions, photos, logos, testimonials and contact details early. Real photographs of your work and team build more trust than generic stock images.</p>
<p>If writing is a struggle, list the questions customers ask you most often and answer them plainly. Those answers make excellent page content and FAQ sections.</p>
<h2>Make it fast and easy on mobile</h2>
<p>Most visitors will open your site on a phone. Check that text is readable without zooming, buttons are easy to tap and pages load quickly on an average connection. Compress images and avoid heavy effects that do not help visitors.</p>
<h2>Plan for search from the start</h2>
<p>Use one clear H1 per page, descriptive page titles and short meta descriptions. Give each service its own page instead of squeezing everything onto one. Our <a href="/it-services/web-development.html">web development team</a> builds this structure in from the beginning, and <a href="/it-services/digital-marketing.html">digital marketing</a> can take it further once the site is live.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>How many pages should a small business website have?</h3>
<p>Most small business websites work well with five to ten pages: home, about, individual service pages, projects or testimonials, and contact.</p>
<h3>What should I prepare before starting a website?</h3>
<p>Prepare your logo, service descriptions, photos, contact details, testimonials and a clear goal for the website.</p>$q$, $q$Web Development$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$How to Plan a Business Website That Gets Enquiries | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$A practical checklist for planning a business website: goals, pages, content, speed and calls to action, from the web team at Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-02T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$UI vs UX Design: What’s the Difference and Why It Matters$q$, $q$ui-vs-ux-difference$q$, $q$UI is how a product looks; UX is how it works for the person using it. Here is how the two fit together.$q$, $q$<h2>What is UX design?</h2>
<p>UX stands for user experience. It covers the whole journey a person has with a website, app or software: can they find what they need, understand what to do next and complete their task without frustration?</p>
<p>UX work includes understanding users, organising information, mapping flows and testing whether real people can use the result.</p>
<h2>What is UI design?</h2>
<p>UI stands for user interface. It is the visible layer: layouts, colours, typography, buttons, icons and the small details of how elements look and respond. Good UI makes the product feel clear, consistent and trustworthy.</p>
<h2>How they work together</h2>
<p>A beautiful interface that is hard to navigate fails, and a logical flow that looks unprofessional loses trust. UX decides what goes where and why; UI gives it a form people can understand at a glance.</p>
<ul><li>UX asks: what does the user need, and what is the easiest path?</li><li>UI asks: how should this look and feel so the path is obvious?</li></ul>
<h2>When does a business need UI/UX design?</h2>
<p>Consider design help when visitors leave your site without contacting you, when customers keep asking how to do simple tasks, or when you are planning a new app or internal tool. Testing ideas on a clickable prototype is far cheaper than fixing a finished product.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/it-services/ui-ux-design.html">UI/UX design service</a> covers research, wireframes, visual design and prototypes, and can lead directly into <a href="/it-services/web-development.html">web development</a>.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is UI/UX design?</h3>
<p>UI/UX design is the practice of designing how a digital product looks (UI) and how it works for users (UX) so that it is clear, usable and pleasant.</p>
<h3>Do I need both UI and UX?</h3>
<p>Yes. UX makes sure the product is useful and easy to use; UI makes it visually clear and consistent. They work best together.</p>$q$, $q$UI/UX Design$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$UI vs UX Design: What Is the Difference? | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$UI and UX are often confused. Learn what each means, how they work together and when your business needs them. A guide from Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-04T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$Local SEO Basics for Small Businesses in Tamil Nadu$q$, $q$local-seo-basics$q$, $q$People search “near me” every day. Here are the basics of showing up when local customers look for what you offer.$q$, $q$<h2>Claim and complete your Google Business Profile</h2>
<p>Your Google Business Profile is often the first thing local customers see. Claim it, choose the right categories, add your address, phone, opening hours, services and real photos. Keep the details up to date.</p>
<h2>Keep your business details consistent</h2>
<p>Use exactly the same name, address and phone number on your website, social media and any directory listings. Inconsistent details confuse both customers and search engines.</p>
<h2>Collect and answer reviews</h2>
<p>Reviews influence both rankings and trust. Politely ask satisfied customers to leave a review and reply to every review, positive or negative, professionally.</p>
<h2>Create useful service pages</h2>
<p>Give each main service its own page that explains what you offer, who it is for and where you work. Mention the areas you serve naturally, where it is true, rather than repeating place names again and again.</p>
<h2>Be patient and measure</h2>
<p>Local SEO builds over months. Track calls, direction requests and website visits from your profile and Google Search Console, and adjust. Our <a href="/it-services/digital-marketing.html">digital marketing team</a> can set up tracking and handle the ongoing work.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is local SEO?</h3>
<p>Local SEO is optimising your online presence so that your business appears in search results and maps for people looking for services near them.</p>
<h3>Is a website necessary for local SEO?</h3>
<p>A Google Business Profile helps, but a website with clear service pages, contact details and good content gives search engines and customers much more to trust.</p>$q$, $q$Digital Marketing$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$Local SEO Basics for Small Businesses | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$How small businesses can rank in local search: Google Business Profile, reviews, service pages and consistent details. Practical steps from Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-06T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$Custom Software vs Off-the-Shelf: How to Choose$q$, $q$custom-software-vs-off-the-shelf$q$, $q$Ready-made tools are quick to start; custom software fits your process. How to decide which is right for your business.$q$, $q$<h2>When off-the-shelf software works well</h2>
<p>If your process is standard — basic accounting, email, simple project tracking — an existing product is usually faster and cheaper to adopt. Start here whenever a tool already does what you need with few workarounds.</p>
<h2>Signs you may need custom software</h2>
<p>Custom software becomes worth considering when the tools you use force awkward workarounds.</p>
<ul><li>Staff copy the same data between several tools or spreadsheets</li><li>Your workflow is unusual and no product fits without heavy compromise</li><li>You need to connect several systems into one process</li><li>Licence costs per user keep growing as the team grows</li></ul>
<h2>Compare more than the price</h2>
<p>Off-the-shelf tools have lower upfront cost but ongoing subscriptions and limits on customisation. Custom software has higher upfront cost but can match your process exactly and you control the roadmap. Consider maintenance, training and data ownership too.</p>
<h2>Start small and grow</h2>
<p>You do not have to build everything at once. A good approach is to build the one module that removes the biggest pain first, then extend. Our <a href="/it-services/software-development.html">software development service</a> works in stages like this so value appears early.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>Is custom software more expensive than ready-made software?</h3>
<p>Custom software usually costs more upfront, but it can save money over time if it removes manual work or replaces several subscriptions. The right choice depends on your process and scale.</p>
<h3>Can custom software integrate with tools I already use?</h3>
<p>Yes. Custom systems can connect to payment gateways, messaging, accounting and other tools through APIs.</p>$q$, $q$Software Development$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$Custom Software vs Off-the-Shelf Software | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$Should your business build custom software or buy a ready-made tool? Compare cost, fit, control and speed with this guide from Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-08T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$Native, Cross-Platform or Web App? Choosing the Right Approach$q$, $q$native-vs-cross-platform-apps$q$, $q$Three ways to put your product on a phone, and how to pick between them based on budget, features and audience.$q$, $q$<h2>Native apps</h2>
<p>Native apps are built separately for Android and iOS using each platform’s own tools. They offer the best performance and deepest access to device features, but need two codebases, which increases cost and maintenance.</p>
<h2>Cross-platform apps</h2>
<p>Frameworks such as Flutter and React Native let one codebase run on both Android and iOS. For most business apps — bookings, orders, dashboards, learning — this approach delivers a very good experience at lower cost and faster delivery.</p>
<h2>Web apps and progressive web apps</h2>
<p>A web app runs in the browser and needs no store approval. It suits tools used mainly on desktop or where installation is not essential. Progressive web apps add offline support and home-screen icons, though device access is more limited than native.</p>
<h2>How to decide</h2>
<p>Ask three questions: does the app need heavy device features such as advanced camera or Bluetooth handling? Which platforms do your users actually use? What is your budget and timeline for the first version?</p>
<p>If you are unsure, our <a href="/it-services/mobile-app-development.html">mobile app development team</a> can recommend an approach after a short discussion of your requirements, and a <a href="/it-services/ui-ux-design.html">prototype</a> helps validate the idea before development.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>Is a cross-platform app as good as a native app?</h3>
<p>For many business apps, yes. Cross-platform apps can deliver smooth performance and a native-like experience. Native still has an edge for very demanding or hardware-heavy apps.</p>
<h3>Do I need an app or is a website enough?</h3>
<p>If customers mainly need information or simple forms, a responsive website may be enough. An app suits frequent use, notifications, or features that benefit from device capabilities.</p>$q$, $q$Mobile App Development$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$Native vs Cross-Platform vs Web Apps | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$Compare native, cross-platform and web apps for your business: cost, speed, performance and features. A plain-language guide from Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-10T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$Website Speed and Core Web Vitals in Plain English$q$, $q$website-speed-core-web-vitals$q$, $q$Slow pages lose visitors. Here is what Core Web Vitals measure and the simple changes that improve them.$q$, $q$<h2>What are Core Web Vitals?</h2>
<p>Core Web Vitals are Google’s measures of how a page feels to use. They focus on three things.</p>
<ul><li>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): how quickly the main content appears</li><li>Interaction to Next Paint (INP): how quickly the page responds when someone taps or clicks</li><li>Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): how much the layout jumps around while loading</li></ul>
<h2>Why speed matters</h2>
<p>Visitors on mobile networks leave slow pages quickly. Faster sites also tend to perform better in search because page experience is one of many signals search engines consider.</p>
<h2>Practical ways to improve speed</h2>
<p>Most speed problems come from a small set of causes.</p>
<ul><li>Resize and compress images, and use modern formats such as WebP</li><li>Load images below the fold lazily</li><li>Remove scripts and plugins you do not use</li><li>Set width and height on images to prevent layout shifts</li><li>Use fast hosting and caching</li></ul>
<h2>Measure before and after</h2>
<p>Use tools such as PageSpeed Insights and the Core Web Vitals report in Google Search Console to see real-world results. If you would like a professional review, our <a href="/it-services/web-development.html">web development team</a> can audit and improve your site’s performance.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What are Core Web Vitals?</h3>
<p>Core Web Vitals are Google metrics measuring loading speed (LCP), responsiveness (INP) and visual stability (CLS) of a web page.</p>
<h3>How can I check my website speed?</h3>
<p>Use Google PageSpeed Insights for a quick test and Google Search Console for real-user Core Web Vitals data.</p>$q$, $q$Technology$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$Website Speed & Core Web Vitals Explained | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$What Core Web Vitals are, why website speed matters for visitors and search, and practical steps to make your site faster. By Creva Solutions.$q$, true, '2026-09-12T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$What to Prepare Before You Start a House Plan$q$, $q$prepare-for-house-plan$q$, $q$A good house plan begins with good information. Gather these details before you meet your designer.$q$, $q$<h2>Know your plot</h2>
<p>Collect the plot dimensions, orientation (which side faces the road and north), road width, and any survey or sale deed drawings. Note existing features such as trees, wells and slopes. Accurate plot information avoids redesign later.</p>
<h2>List your needs, not just room counts</h2>
<p>Think about how your household actually lives.</p>
<ul><li>Number of bedrooms and who uses them</li><li>Space for elders, guests or a home office</li><li>Kitchen style, pooja room and utility area needs</li><li>Parking for cars and two-wheelers</li><li>Plans for adding a floor in future</li></ul>
<h2>Set a realistic budget range</h2>
<p>Share a construction budget range with your designer. It shapes decisions about size, structure and finishes. Keep a buffer for items that often get missed, such as compound wall, sump, septic tank and electrical work.</p>
<h2>Collect reference ideas</h2>
<p>Save photos of houses, façades and interiors you like and note what you like about each. References help communicate taste far better than words.</p>
<h2>Understand the steps that follow</h2>
<p>After the layout is finalised, the plan is developed into dimensioned drawings, 3D views if you want them, structural details and estimates. Our <a href="/civil-services/planning.html">planning services</a> and <a href="/civil-services/civil-design.html">civil design services</a> cover these stages. Approval requirements vary by local authority, so confirm what is needed for your plot early.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What documents do I need to start a house plan?</h3>
<p>Plot dimensions or a survey sketch, orientation, and your requirements and budget range. Ownership documents will be needed for approval submissions.</p>
<h3>Can a house plan be changed after it is finalised?</h3>
<p>Changes are easiest before detailed drawings and construction begin. Later changes are possible but can affect cost and schedule.</p>$q$, $q$Civil Design$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$What to Prepare Before Starting a House Plan | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$A checklist for homeowners planning a new house: plot details, needs, budget and reference ideas that help designers create the right plan.$q$, true, '2026-09-14T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$2D Drafting Explained: Plans, Elevations and Sections$q$, $q$2d-drafting-explained$q$, $q$Floor plans, elevations, sections: what each drawing shows and why builders need all of them.$q$, $q$<h2>What is 2D drafting?</h2>
<p>2D drafting is the creation of flat, scaled technical drawings that describe a building. Today this is done in CAD software such as AutoCAD, which makes drawings accurate and easy to revise.</p>
<h2>The main drawings in a set</h2>
<p>A typical drawing set includes several views, each answering a different question.</p>
<ul><li>Floor plan: a view from above showing room layout, walls, doors and windows</li><li>Elevation: the outside view of each face of the building</li><li>Section: a vertical cut showing heights, floors, slabs and stairs</li><li>Site plan: the building’s position within the plot</li><li>Working details: close-ups for construction such as stairs, sunshades and toilets</li></ul>
<h2>Why accuracy and consistency matter</h2>
<p>If a plan and elevation disagree, the contractor has to guess. Consistent dimensions, levels and annotations across every sheet prevent expensive errors on site.</p>
<h2>Getting drawings prepared</h2>
<p>You can begin with a hand sketch, a measurement of an existing building or a concept from a designer. Our <a href="/civil-services/2d-drafting.html">2D drafting service</a> converts these into clean drawing sets, and our <a href="/civil-services/3d-modeling.html">3D modeling</a> team can show you how the design will look.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is 2D drafting?</h3>
<p>2D drafting is creating flat, dimensioned technical drawings — such as plans, elevations and sections — that describe how a building is arranged and built.</p>
<h3>What is the difference between a plan and an elevation?</h3>
<p>A plan is a top-down view of a floor layout. An elevation is a straight-on view of the outside face of the building.</p>$q$, $q$2D Drafting$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$2D Drafting Explained: Plans, Elevations, Sections | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$What 2D drafting is and what drawings you need for construction: floor plans, elevations, sections and working drawings, explained simply.$q$, true, '2026-09-16T09:00:00+05:30'),
($q$3D Modeling: See Your Building Before You Build It$q$, $q$3d-modeling-before-you-build$q$, $q$A 3D model lets you walk around your future home on screen. Here is what it shows and why it saves money.$q$, $q$<h2>What a 3D model shows</h2>
<p>A 3D model is a digital version of the building with volumes, openings, materials and lighting. From it, we produce still images or walkthrough views from any angle, so you understand proportions in a way plans alone cannot show.</p>
<h2>Benefits for homeowners</h2>
<p>Most people find it hard to imagine a building from a set of lines. Seeing it in 3D removes that difficulty.</p>
<ul><li>Compare façade styles and colour schemes before committing</li><li>Check that rooms, heights and openings feel right</li><li>Share the design easily with family and contractors</li><li>Spot problems on screen instead of on site</li></ul>
<h2>How a 3D model is made</h2>
<p>A model starts from accurate 2D plans and elevations. Materials, colours, landscaping and lighting are then added and the chosen views are rendered. Changes are much quicker to explore in a model than in a built structure.</p>
<h2>What you need to start</h2>
<p>You need a plan or dimensions of the building and any reference images for style. If you do not have plans yet, our <a href="/civil-services/planning.html">planning</a> and <a href="/civil-services/2d-drafting.html">2D drafting</a> services can create them, and then our <a href="/civil-services/3d-modeling.html">3D modeling service</a> can visualise the result.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>What is 3D modeling in architecture?</h3>
<p>3D modeling is building a digital three-dimensional representation of a building so its shape, materials and lighting can be viewed before construction.</p>
<h3>Will the 3D render look exactly like the finished building?</h3>
<p>Renders closely represent the design and chosen materials, but real-world lighting, site conditions and construction finishes can cause small differences.</p>$q$, $q$3D Modeling$q$, 'Creva Solutions', $q$3D Modeling for Homes: See Before You Build | Creva Solutions$q$, $q$How 3D models and elevation renders help homeowners choose designs, compare options and avoid costly changes during construction.$q$, true, '2026-09-18T09:00:00+05:30')
